<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sikh Confederacy</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Sikh confederacies</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sikhism">Sikh</a> Confederacy refers to the group of Sikh misls, or confederate clans, that governed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/punjab">Punjab</a> after the decline of Mughal authority in the eighteenth century. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ranjit-singh">Ranjit Singh</a>, born into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sukerchakia-misl">Sukerchakia misl</a>, unified them into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sikh-empire">Sikh Empire</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maratha-empire">Maratha Empire</a> profile mentions the Sikh confederacies among the powers with which the Marathas dealt.</p></div>
